WEBVTT

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:02.390
<i>It is the 25th year of the Taisho Era.</i>

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:08.150
<i>Shiginuma Takashi informs the girl that 
there is a member of Karasu in Fukurou.</i>

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:12.570
<i>Unable to cope with those 
words, the girl breaks down.</i>

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:16.750
<i>Kougami Akira confesses to her 
that he is the one from Karasu,</i>

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.870
<i>to protect her from its ill intent.</i>

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.220
<i>This is the story of Kuze 
Tsugumi and her sympathy.</i>

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:08.770
Why?

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.270
Why did you go after Kuze?!

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.880
Putting crow feathers in my stuff without my—

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:16.850
Silence!

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:26.660
Don't look away.

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:29.140
Get a good look at it.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.920
Just like the blood that poured out last time...

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:35.920
S-Stop it!

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:41.440
No matter how hard you struggle,

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:44.930
you can never escape from me.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:59.450
The Colors of the Flames of Love

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:59.450
-Tragedy-

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:07.900
The rumor that there was a Karasu spy in 
Fukurou has been around for some time.

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:14.170
But I believed it couldn't possibly 
be one of the members here.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:16.610
This was my own fault.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:18.980
There has to be some kind of mistake!

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:22.590
Even if it is true, Akira must 
have had some reason...

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:26.460
Regardless of his reasons, 
now that it's come to this,

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:28.600
we have to accept it as truth.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.820
Ukai-kun is right.

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:34.100
For us to get unsettled over this 
is just what Karasu wants.

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:38.360
There's only one good way 
for us to handle this.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:41.960
We must track down Karasu as 
soon as possible and crush them.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:44.680
Without forgetting to protect 
the princess, of course.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:50.620
We also can't overlook the fact that 
Shiginuma is trying to bring Kuze into Karasu.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:55.380
Kuze, I don't want you acting
alone if you can avoid it.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.020
Yes, ma'am.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.880
<b>Imperial Capital University Hospital</b>

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:06.890
Hello there.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:11.020
Oh, Nee-san! Did you bring 
the book I asked for?

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:15.070
Who's that guy?

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:17.960
There's no need to be so rude, Hitaki.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:21.170
This is my senpai from 
Fukurou, Ozaki Hayato-san.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:22.350
Nice to meet you, Hitaki-kun.

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:24.020
Why did you come here?

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:25.910
What are you to my sister?

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.300
Hitaki, don't be so rude.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.410
I'm acting as your sister's guard for today.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:37.170
Guard? Why is she being guarded?

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:39.340
We're on a top secret mission.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:42.920
I can't give any details, 
but there's no need to worry.

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:49.180
You don't seem very dependable.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:51.660
And your clothes are all sloppy.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:53.030
Now, Hitaki...

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:54.900
Be careful, Nee-san.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:58.360
I bet he's just trying to seduce you.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:04:59.420
Hitaki!

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:01.680
That's why his chest is exposed like that.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:02.770
What do you mean?

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:06.070
The marriage fraudster 
in Migiwa-sensei's book,

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:08.350
<i>The Vow of the Twilight Moon</i>, 
dressed like that, too.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:10.240
Stop it, Hitaki!

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:15.190
I'd better get going, Hitaki. 
I'll visit again soon.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:17.720
Please be careful, Nee-san.

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:21.840
Thank you, but rest assured, 
the members of Fukurou are with me.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:22.710
Bye.

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:27.300
Sorry for the wait, Hayato.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.320
Hayato?

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:33.220
Ready to go?

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:49.490
Um... I'm really sorry 
my brother was so rude.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:51.730
That's not it.

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:52.740
What's not it?

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.140
Nothing, never mind.

00:05:56.710 --> 00:06:00.540
Anyway, I'm really glad 
Hitaki-kun has recovered so well.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.750
It looks like he won't even have many scars.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:04.520
Thank you.

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:07.920
We have to make sure there won't be any other

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:09.860
victims of cursed tomes, like him.

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:25.890
Is he still being held captive?

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:29.160
I won't tell you to forget about him,

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:31.660
but you have the right to be happy, too.

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:35.480
I know. That's why, when this case is over,

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:37.710
I'm going to get over this and—

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:41.230
Whoa! You gotta be careful with that line.

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:46.670
"When this war is over, I'm going 
to go back home and get married."

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:48.040
Excuse me?

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:55.330
I read a story recently where a soldier was
killed by enemy fire after saying that.

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:58.180
Don't joke about that. You'll jinx me.

00:06:58.990 --> 00:07:00.190
I'm being serious.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:05.910
There's the string of unnatural deaths
surrounding Prime Minister Ukai recently,

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:08.430
plus this incident with 
Kougami-kun and Karasu.

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:11.450
You don't know when something 
might happen to you.

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:13.580
What about you?

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:17.050
You've been snooping around 
in all kinds of places lately.

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:19.220
Getting in too deep is dangerous.

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:22.560
I'm living my life so that I don't 
have any regrets when I do die.

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:25.560
It's people like that who live the longest.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:27.460
I'm not so sure about that.

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:31.470
Actually, I've heard a bit 
of an interesting rumor.

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:38.220
Someone at the Imperial Capital University 
is trying to make artificial cursed tomes.

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:40.960
Please tell me everything.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:43.460
It's not quite the time to
talk about it just yet.

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:47.100
Once I get confirmation, 
you'll be the first one I report to.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:48.750
Senpai.

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:49.740
What is it?

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:55.020
I saw a movie recently where a police 
reporter was killed after saying that.

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:06.880
Still investigating things at this hour?

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:11.900
I figured I should study a bit more, 
since I'm also part of Fukurou.

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:14.860
Our research on the cursed 
tomes is ongoing,

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:16.890
so there's still much that we don't know.

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:22.920
There's an old historical record that says,

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:28.770
"In books, I could see something other
than letters, and I could hear voices."

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:31.950
Which means the burning 
of books due to fears

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:34.780
that their words held powers
has been around for ages.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:37.820
Recent research has advanced

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:42.910
the idea that it may be a kind of
superpower humans possess.

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:44.380
A superpower?

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:46.280
If I could see auras, too,

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:50.500
I might be able to investigate and 
research things in more depth.

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:53.310
Excuse me.

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:21.930
Nabari-san?

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:24.710
Nabari-san, are you all right?

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:30.210
Are you all right, Nabari-san?

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:33.190
You seemed to be having a nightmare...

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:37.790
Yes, I was just dreaming of the past.

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:39.220
Dreaming of the past?

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:42.150
Anyway, what brings you here at this hour?

00:09:42.150 --> 00:09:45.440
I'm sorry. I was investigating 
the cursed tomes.

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:48.480
Also, I made more marmalade, 
so I brought you some.

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:51.480
Thanks for always doing this.

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:52.820
Not at all.

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:57.920
That's the cursed tome Hitaki read, isn't it?

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:04.500
<b>Nozaki 
Youji</b>

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:06.300
Nozaki Youji...

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:12.000
I looked into it. There wasn't a single book,
including printed books, by the same author.

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:16.200
If the same author wrote them,
would their auras be the same color?

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:17.890
Not necessarily.

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:22.700
The aura color changes based on the emotions 
put into the book, and their intensity.

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:35.530
Oh, that's a newly written 
manuscript by a certain author.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:37.920
If the author writes it by hand,

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:40.530
it'll still become cursed, 
even if it isn't a bound book.

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:44.530
What matters most are the 
strong emotions put into it.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:48.410
So long as it has that, even a simple 
letter can become a cursed tome.

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:50.110
Even a letter?

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:00.220
What's this?

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:05.340
What the hell?

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:24.530
Yoshikiri-senpai!

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:28.290
Huh? What's the matter, Masaki?

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:35.550
Jeez, I heard you hadn't gone home 
and—ugh, you reek of alcohol!

00:11:35.550 --> 00:11:38.170
Yeah, I was out late drinking with Hayato.

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:40.560
I rushed over here because I was worried.

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:41.670
Why?

00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:44.920
Since you said yesterday that you 
were going out to drink, I thought...

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:46.680
Thought what?

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:50.260
An unidentified dead body 
was found downtown.

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:54.190
Wait, Senpai! Where are you going?

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:56.030
Gathering info, obviously!

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:58.020
Honestly...

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:03.220
The victim's identity is being 
kept out of the newspapers,

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:05.090
but it was a police officer.

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:08.600
He was doing an undercover 
investigation in Nachtigal,

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:11.720
but we had been unable to get in 
touch with him since last week.

00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:13.080
Was he murdered?

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:15.340
He was pecked to death by crows.

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:18.960
Oh, I'm referring to actual crows, 
not the organization.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:21.010
The damage was so severe that

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:23.970
the cause of death has yet to be 
determined, but it is likely.

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:25.960
What about Shiginuma?

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:28.700
He hasn't made any conspicuous 
movements as of now,

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:31.350
but it would be wise to exercise caution.

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:34.330
There's also the issue 
with the prime minister,

00:12:34.330 --> 00:12:36.230
so you should be careful, too, Ukai-san.

00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:38.230
I-I'm fine.

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:42.330
So long as you're staying in this 
building, we'll protect you.

00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:44.080
And I am with you, as well.

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:45.680
Oh, be careful.

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:47.760
Please wait three more minutes.

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:50.680
It's too hot. It might burn your 
sensitive tongue, young master.

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:51.380
You'll need to be even more 
careful now, too, my princess.

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:52.180
Don't call me that!

00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:58.880
What's this about?

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:03.480
Sorry about this. Shizuru-san 
insisted on coming with me.

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:06.730
It's dangerous for the 
princess to be on her own.

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:08.340
Shizuru-san, please!

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:10.890
I feel like that's dangerous in another way...

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:13.050
But this works out well.

00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:16.140
I would love for Migiwa-sensei 
to hear what I have to say, too.

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:20.150
It would be my pleasure to be 
of use to such a lovely lady.

00:13:22.490 --> 00:13:26.400
The truth is, well... 
There's someone that I like.

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:30.060
I see. So you need romantic advice.

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:32.410
In that case, I am indeed 
the right person.

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:37.000
Now, tell us all about the dreams 
of a sweet maiden in love.

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:38.240
<i>All the characters in Shizuru-san's 
books die at the end, though...</i>

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:39.420
<i>Will this be okay?</i>

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:43.640
He's always working, so he 
never seems to notice me...

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:47.890
But the way he gets engrossed in his work 
is part of what makes him so great.

00:13:48.730 --> 00:13:52.830
He's been getting involved in some 
dangerous cases lately, though...

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:56.430
Would this happen to be Hayato's 
senpai, Yoshikiri-kun?

00:13:56.650 --> 00:13:58.810
H-How did you know?!

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:01.710
Even I could figure that out, Koruri-chan.

00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:02.940
No way!

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:07.440
Well, whoever the man is, 
I only have one word of advice.

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:10.570
As the song goes, "Life is short, 
so love, young maidens."

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:14.720
If you've fallen for him, you need to 
start by telling him how you feel.

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:16.580
But how do I...

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:20.580
Well, what about... a love letter?

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:23.850
A love letter? That might work!

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:26.830
Maybe I'll confess my feelings 
once this case is over...

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:31.210
If you want to know how to write a 
love letter that will melt a man's heart,

00:14:31.210 --> 00:14:32.880
I can teach you anytime.

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:35.330
I'll look forward to your help, then!

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:37.730
I'll be rooting for you 
and Yoshikiri-san, too.

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:39.140
Thank you!

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:42.230
Don't you have anyone like 
that yourself, Tsugumi-chan?

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:46.040
She does, see? He's right in front of you.

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:47.430
Huh? Is this true?

00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:51.220
What are you talking about, 
Shizuru-san?! That's not true!

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:54.580
What, it's not? So who is it, then?

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:56.240
Well, I mean...

00:14:56.760 --> 00:15:00.250
I'm too focused on work right now.
I don't have time for love.

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:03.250
<b>Imperial Capital 
University</b>

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:47.280
I want you to see if this 
is a cursed tome or not.

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:48.550
Well, Kuze?

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:52.050
I can't see an aura.

00:15:52.690 --> 00:15:54.670
What about you, Nabari-san?

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:57.060
Unfortunately, this isn't a cursed tome.

00:15:58.670 --> 00:15:59.950
Where did you get this?

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:01.820
Just don't ask.

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:04.560
The police would consider it
theft if they found out.

00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:09.320
Damn it. I'll definitely get 
some kind of proof next time.

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:12.920
You really shouldn't do anything 
too reckless, Yoshikiri-san.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:16.870
You've always been the type to 
overdo things, even back in school.

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.110
Really?

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:19.830
Yoshikiri-san is Hayato's senpai.

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:19.830
Did you forget?

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:23.720
Like when you said something about 
traveling across Japan and left for a month.

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:22.060
That explains it.

00:16:23.720 --> 00:16:25.880
Oh, yeah. I forgot about that.

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:28.630
It was a total bust, though.

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:28.630
I've always thought they 
seemed rather similar.

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:33.540
Yoshikiri-san, please try not 
to do anything reckless.

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:35.470
Koruri-chan has been worried about you, too.

00:16:35.740 --> 00:16:37.720
There are two ways to be reckless.

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:39.470
One is to do it and then regret it.

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:41.470
The other is to not do it and regret it.

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:45.490
You've always been the type 
to not do it, then regret it.

00:16:45.490 --> 00:16:47.310
You're bringing that up again?

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:48.130
Again?

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:51.580
The impregnable park princess.

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:52.990
Park princess?

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:57.240
Yes, the first girl Hayato fell in love with.

00:16:57.520 --> 00:16:58.200
Huh?

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:00.700
Senpai, this really isn't the time...

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:04.460
Why not? Kuze-san should 
hear about this, too.

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:06.010
Please stop.

00:17:06.010 --> 00:17:08.000
Aw, don't be shy.

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:13.510
The princess was always sitting on 
a park bench reading by herself.

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:19.080
One day, Hayato happened to be passing by 
when he fell in love with her at first sight.

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:21.390
From then on, he took the long way

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:25.640
to the university every day 
to pass by the park.

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:27.240
Just go!

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:28.450
I can't!

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:29.320
Just go!

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:30.860
I told you, I can't!

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:32.980
Why not? Why won't you just do it now?

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:34.150
Why does it matter?

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:41.160
Was she "impregnable," or did you 
just not even try to approach her?

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:45.440
Other guys at school would 
ask her out on dates,

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:48.300
but they all got flat-out rejected.

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:50.840
She may have given in if 
you'd approached her.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:52.420
Please don't tease me.

00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:56.670
So, what ended up happening with her?

00:17:56.900 --> 00:18:00.420
Let Hayato tell you that himself. See ya.

00:18:06.610 --> 00:18:11.030
He might talk big, but he was a late
bloomer with women, too.

00:18:11.030 --> 00:18:12.210
Really?

00:18:12.210 --> 00:18:17.680
Oh, that reminds me. He was telling me 
that he found a letter in his bag earlier.

00:18:17.680 --> 00:18:20.320
A letter from an unknown sender.

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:21.720
Maybe it's a love letter.

00:18:22.440 --> 00:18:23.620
Love letter?

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:26.040
<i>Could it be from Koruri-chan?</i>

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:29.780
<i>But she said she would wait 
until this case was over.</i>

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:34.700
Something the matter?

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:40.220
No. Anyway, what ended up happening 
with the impregnable park princess?

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:42.580
Nothing happened.

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:45.240
Ultimately, I was never 
able to confess to her.

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:47.980
Even if I had confessed to 
her and been successful,

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:51.000
it didn't feel right being the
only one allowed to be happy.

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:56.230
I had a little sister.

00:18:57.240 --> 00:18:59.020
She was like Hitaki-kun.

00:18:59.020 --> 00:19:00.760
One day, she read a Japanese-style book and...

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:11.250
Fortunately, her life was spared,

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:15.110
but horrible burn scars remained on her face.

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:16.750
Agonized by that, my sister...

00:19:28.240 --> 00:19:29.700
I'm so sorry.

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:34.770
I had no idea, and I made you come 
along with me to visit Hitaki.

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:37.960
There's nothing to apologize for. 
Don't worry about it.

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:39.010
But...

00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:42.710
Anyway, that's the reason 
I couldn't confess to her.

00:19:43.250 --> 00:19:47.600
At the time, I thought that I shouldn't 
be the only one able to be happy.

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:53.530
Besides, it was around that time that 
talk of studying abroad came up,

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:55.480
and I left Japan for a while.

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:57.300
When I got back, I joined Fukurou.

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:02.720
To prevent other tragedies like 
my sister's from happening again.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:04.800
<i>Just like me...</i>

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:07.660
Actually, Tokimiya-san is the same, too.

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:13.520
Her husband read a Japanese-style 
book and burned to death.

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:15.390
I had no idea...

00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:18.020
Uh... Good evening.

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:20.030
Koruri-chan?

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:22.560
What brings you here so late?

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:27.730
Yoshikiri-senpai said he was going 
to stop by Fukurou, so I, uh...

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:29.540
brought some snacks.

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:32.610
He actually just left here.

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:35.040
You just missed him.

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:37.040
Oh, darn...

00:20:37.780 --> 00:20:40.170
Hey, did you write that 
letter to Yoshikiri-san?

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:41.550
What are you talking about?

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:46.300
Even a simple letter can 
become a cursed tome.

00:20:50.330 --> 00:20:51.060
Kuze!

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:53.060
Nishidera Avenue

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:54.590
The prince of the university.

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:55.190
Prince?

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:59.690
He saved me when I got hurt in the street.

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:02.420
He took a look at your scraped 
knees, too, didn't he?

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:03.200
Yeah!

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:04.700
Hey, Kuze!

00:21:16.180 --> 00:21:17.460
Don't read that!

00:21:20.080 --> 00:21:21.460
Hey, what the hell...

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:22.890
But you don't know his name, right?

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:24.470
Just that he goes to the Imperial University.

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:29.040
You'll have to fall down again.

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:30.300
Totally.

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:35.480
Run... ...ay...

00:21:35.740 --> 00:21:38.260
Excuse me... You dropped your bag.

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:44.450
Run... away...

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:49.990
Hurry, Igarashi-san!

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:50.990
Shiratori-san!

00:22:05.600 --> 00:22:09.820
No!

00:23:20.480 --> 00:23:23.560
<i>Hello, my princess. This is Migiwa Shizuru.</i>

00:23:21.170 --> 00:23:36.430
Chapter 9:  "Dance of the Evil Bird -Karasu-"

00:23:23.560 --> 00:23:25.080
<i>Love is a splendid thing.</i>

00:23:25.080 --> 00:23:27.510
<i>It's the magic that makes 
women more beautiful.</i>

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:31.090
<i>Although, I guess this isn't 
the time to talk about that.</i>

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:33.640
<i>We have a big case to take care of.</i>

00:23:33.640 --> 00:23:38.470
<i>But once this is over, I'll take my 
time teaching you about adult love.</i>
